  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Migrations keep the indexes and constraints a column change used to drop or rebuild: Changed answers in 5.6.0 (https://github.com/CaffeinatedCoder/EFCore.ComplexIndexes/blob/v5.6.0/docs/upgrading.md#changed-answers-in-560).\n\nChanged answers\n\n- Migrations: moving a table into the default schema keeps the complex indexes and constraints on it. They were dropped and created again, and on PostgreSQL, where Npgsql leaves such a table in its schema, the migration failed (42P01) (#185 (https://github.com/CaffeinatedCoder/EFCore.ComplexIndexes/issues/185), Upgrading (https://github.com/CaffeinatedCoder/EFCore.ComplexIndexes/blob/v5.6.0/docs/upgrading.md#a-move-into-the-default-schema-keeps-what-is-on-the-table)).\n- Migrations: on SQL Server, changing only a column's default value, default SQL or comment keeps the complex indexes on it. Each was dropped and created again around the change, which issues no ALTER COLUMN (#186 (https://github.com/CaffeinatedCoder/EFCore.ComplexIndexes/issues/186), Upgrading (https://github.com/CaffeinatedCoder/EFCore.ComplexIndexes/blob/v5.6.0/docs/upgrading.md#a-default-or-comment-change-keeps-the-index-on-sql-server)).\n- Migrations: renaming a column keeps the complex indexes, exclusion constraints and temporal constraints that read it, and renames a default name that includes the column. They were dropped and created again around the rename. SQL Server still re-creates an index whose filter reads the column (#182 (https://github.com/CaffeinatedCoder/EFCore.ComplexIndexes/issues/182), Upgrading (https://github.com/CaffeinatedCoder/EFCore.ComplexIndexes/blob/v5.6.0/docs/upgrading.md#a-column-rename-keeps-what-reads-the-column)).\n\nFixed\n\n- Indexes: on SQL Server, a complex index whose filter or INCLUDE entry names a column in another case, [note] for Note, is dropped before an ALTER COLUMN or rename of that column and created after it, where the migration failed at apply, since SQL Server rejects either while the index exists (Msg 5074 for ALTER COLUMN) (#189 (https://github.com/CaffeinatedCoder/EFCore.ComplexIndexes/issues/189)).\n\nFull changelog: https://github.com/CaffeinatedCoder/EFCore.ComplexIndexes/blob/v5.6.0/src/EFCore.ComplexIndexes.SqlServer/CHANGELOG.md",
